    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "In table order: $-5^\\circ\\mathrm{C},\\ -5^\\circ\\mathrm{C},\\ 4^\\circ\\mathrm{C},\\ 15^\\circ\\mathrm{C},\\ 5^\\circ\\mathrm{C},\\ 9^\\circ\\mathrm{C}$.\n\nA negative result means it is warmer outside than inside.",
      "worked": "Subtract the outside temperature from the inside temperature. When subtracting a negative integer, add its opposite.\n\nMonday: $20-25=-5^\\circ\\mathrm{C}$.\n\nTuesday: $13-18=-5^\\circ\\mathrm{C}$.\n\nWednesday: $24-20=4^\\circ\\mathrm{C}$.\n\nThursday:\n$$\\begin{align*}10-(-5)&=10+5\\\\10-(-5)&=15^\\circ\\mathrm{C}.\\end{align*}$$\nFriday:\n$$\\begin{align*}-5-(-10)&=-5+10\\\\-5-(-10)&=5^\\circ\\mathrm{C}.\\end{align*}$$\nSaturday:\n$$\\begin{align*}3-(-6)&=3+6\\\\3-(-6)&=9^\\circ\\mathrm{C}.\\end{align*}$$\nA negative result means the inside temperature is lower than the outside temperature, so it is warmer outside.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
